<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="distraction.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="distraction">
    <!-- Tier 1 screen #4 (distraction_manager_gui::show). The first toggle-list
         shape: a moving-cursor list whose rows mutate in place (CONFIRM flips
         Enabled/Disabled), plus a description header that re-renders as the
         cursor moves. Keyboard stays on input_context (UP/DOWN move, CONFIRM
         toggles, QUIT saves+exits); RmlUi renders + handles mouse only. The
         model is live-synced every redraw (see sync_rml in the .cpp), so the
         cursor highlight + per-row status + header description all track the
         selection without per-branch DirtyVariable calls. Selection highlight
         via .item.selected (theme); status colour rides inside status_rml via
         cata_text_to_rml. -->
    <div class="panel dm-panel">
        <div class="dm-header" data-rml="desc_rml"></div>

        <div class="dm-list scroll-pane">
            <div class="item dm-row" data-for="row : rows"
                 data-class-selected="row.selected"
                 data-event-mouseover="on_select(it_index)"
                 data-event-click="on_select(it_index)">
                <span class="dm-name" data-rml="row.name_rml"></span>
                <span class="dm-status" data-rml="row.status_rml"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
